From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Levickij <plevickij57@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 23:50:49 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm: finalize Hikari DSI transfer path

Preserve the final source-backed MSM8x60 display corrections used by the
active Hikari tree: the DSI byte-clock root, system/MMSS fabric path and FPB
votes, low-address per-transfer command DMA mapping, Sony PLL register order,
and non-continuous panel clock policy.

This patch is intentionally applied after the project's strict historical
source transforms, because its preimage includes those corrections.

Signed-off-by: Paul Levickij <plevickij57@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/clk/qcom/mmcc-msm8660.c               |  30 +++-
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi.h                 |   8 +-
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_cfg.h             |   5 +-
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c            | 144 +++++++++++++++---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy_45nm.c    |  16 +-
 .../panel/panel-renesas-r63306-tmd-mdv22.c    |  10 +-
 drivers/interconnect/qcom/msm8660.c           |   3 +-
 7 files changed, 179 insertions(+), 37 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/mmcc-msm8660.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/mmcc-msm8660.c
index fda2dabda..83dd9e740 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/mmcc-msm8660.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/mmcc-msm8660.c
@@ -623,7 +623,14 @@ static struct clk_branch dsi1_clk = {
 static struct clk_branch dsi1_byte_clk = {
 	.halt_check = BRANCH_HALT_DELAY,
 	.clkr = {
-		.enable_reg = 0x0058,
+		/*
+		 * Unlike the escape clock branches in MISC_CC_REG, the DSI byte
+		 * clock is an RCG whose root enable is MISC_CC2_REG bit 2.  The
+		 * downstream MSM8x60 clock driver models the same register as its
+		 * ns_reg and root_en_mask.  Bits 27:24 hold the divider and bit 0
+		 * selects the DSI PHY PLL; probe initializes those to /1 and PLL.
+		 */
+		.enable_reg = 0x005c,
 		.enable_mask = BIT(2),
 		.hw.init = &(struct clk_init_data){
 			.name = "dsi1_byte_clk",
@@ -2946,6 +2953,7 @@ static int mmcc_msm8660_unhalt_fabric_ports(struct device *dev)
 	struct qcom_rpm *rpm;
 	/* halt_data[0]=0 = CLK_UNHALT for all bits; halt_data[1] = port mask */
 	u32 mmss_halt[2] = {0, GENMASK(13, 0)};
+	u32 sys_halt[2] = {0, BIT(13)};
 	int rc;
 
 	rpm_node = of_find_compatible_node(NULL, NULL, "qcom,rpm-msm8660");
@@ -2981,8 +2989,24 @@ static int mmcc_msm8660_unhalt_fabric_ports(struct device *dev)
 			    QCOM_RPM_MM_FABRIC_HALT, mmss_halt, 2);
 	if (rc)
 		dev_err(dev, "MMSS fabric unhalt failed: %d\n", rc);
-	else
-		dev_info(dev, "MMSS fabric: unhalted all master ports (0-13)\n");
+	else {
+		/*
+		 * DSI command DMA is an AHB master behind the MMSS FPB.  Its
+		 * memory reads leave MMSS through system-fabric master port 13,
+		 * rather than through one of the multimedia AXI master ports
+		 * above.  The downstream bus driver unhalts this port when the
+		 * MMSS-FPB path is requested; the DSI V2 binding has no ICC path,
+		 * so make that legacy requirement explicit here for bring-up.
+		 */
+		rc = qcom_rpm_write(rpm, QCOM_RPM_ACTIVE_STATE,
+				    QCOM_RPM_SYS_FABRIC_HALT, sys_halt, 2);
+		if (rc)
+			dev_err(dev, "system MMSS-FPB master unhalt failed: %d\n",
+				rc);
+		else
+			dev_info(dev,
+				 "MMSS fabric ports and system MMSS-FPB master unhalted\n");
+	}
 
 	put_device(&rpm_pdev->dev);
 
